    "title": "Duke Defeats Arizona State in Sun Bowl",
    "text": "• Duke defeated Arizona State 42-39 in the Sun Bowl.\n• Darian Mensah, Duke's quarterback, threw for 327 yards and four touchdowns, earning MVP honors.\n• Mensah completed 29 of 51 passes with one interception.\n• Duke achieved its fourth consecutive win.\n• Duke (9-5) won nine games for a second straight season.\n• Arizona State (8-5) was led by quarterback Jeff Sims, who passed for 375 yards and three touchdowns.\n• Sims also ran for 70 yards and two touchdowns.\n• The game set Sun Bowl records for combined total offense (1,158 yards), individual team offense (ASU, 619 yards), and most points in a half (52).\n• The game had three ties and two lead changes.\n• Arizona State took a 39-35 lead in the fourth quarter before Duke regained the lead.\n• Duke's Que’Sean Brown scored a 17-yard touchdown to put Duke ahead 42-39.\n• Duke's Luke Mergott intercepted a pass by Sims to seal the win.\n• Arizona State was without 22 players, including quarterback Sam Leavitt and wide receiver Jordyn Tyson.\n• Duke opens its season at home against Tulane on Sept. 5.\n• Arizona State opens its 2026 season at home against Morgan State on Sept. 5.",
